:R-HSA-936440  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0032480 ;
        rdfs:comment        "As with other cytokine systems, production of type I IFN is a transient process, and can be hazardous to the host if unregulated, resulting in chronic cellular toxicity or inflammatory and autoimmune diseases. RIG-I-mediated production of IFN can, in turn, increase the transcription of RIG-I itself, thus setting into motion an IFN amplification loop, which if left unchecked, could become deleterious to the host. This module mainly focuses on the endogenous negative regulation of the RIG-I-like receptor (RLR) family proteins RIG-I and MDA5." ;
        rdfs:label          "Negative regulators of RIG-I/MDA5 signaling" ;
        dc:contributor      "Reviewed: Kawai, T, Akira, S, 2010-10-30" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Edited: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" , "Authored: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-936440" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-168928/R-HSA-168928> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

